    "chunk_size_bytes": 1794,
    "chunk_text": "Omega Line triumphs at CPM Sri Lanka Management Leadership Excellence Awards 2025\n\nOmega Line, one of Sri Lanka\u2019s largest apparel exporters to Europe, operating under the Oniverse umbrella (formerly Calzedonia),announced that four of its employees have been honoured at the CPM Sri Lanka Management Leadership Excellence Awards 2025, further cementing its reputation for cultivating outstanding leadership within the apparel sector.\n\nNotably, Sampath Weerakoon, Chief HR Officer \u2013 Operations, not only emerged winner in the Apparel & Garment Sector \u2013 Corporate Management Level but also distinguished himself at a national level by clinching the Overall Bronze Award. This accolade builds on his recent recognition among the Top Most HR Leaders in Asia at the 20th Employer Branding Awards, reaffirming his role as a visionary people strategist not just in apparel, but in Sri Lanka\u2019s wider corporate leadership landscape.\n\nHis win is also a reflection of Omega Line\u2019s deep-rooted commitment to cultivating leaders who drive innovation, inclusivity, and sustainable growth, values that continue to strengthen the company\u2019s reputation as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most people-focused apparel exporters.\n\nMeanwhile, Kanishka Weerasinghe, AGM \u2013 Production emerged as first runner-up, while Damien Lekamge, AGM \u2013 Production and Charman Dep, AGM \u2013 Production Planning were both awarded second runner-up in the same category.\n\nCSE to conduct a full day of trading from Disaster Recovery site\n\nSlack expands platform to power secure, context-aware AI apps and agents built on conversational data\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
