    "chunk_text": "Hong Kong-based World Elite Ltd acquires 50.01 per cent ordinary shares in Gestetner of Ceylon; market overall positive\n\nA Hong Kong based entity, World Elite Limited, has acquired 50.01 percent of the issued ordinary shares of Gestetner of Ceylon Plc.\n\nAccording to the CSE, 1,329,115 ordinary shares were bought at Rs 239.75 per share for Rs 318 million (Rs 318,655,321.25).\n\nThe balance 65,920 shares were purchased from the CSE on October 13.\n\nUnder this transaction the company owns more than 50 percent of shares in Gestetner.\n\nAmid those developments, the market performance was overall positive, owing to halt in increasing electricity tariffs for next two months by the Public Utilities Commission.\n\nThis had given an impetus to the market. The All Share Price Index went up by 70.85, while the S and P SL20 rose by 22.07 points.\n\nTurnover stood at Rs 5.74 billion with 13 crossings. Top seven crossings were reported in Hemas Holdings; 4.8 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 159 million; its shares traded at Rs 32.50, Ceylon Land Equity 8.7 million shares crossed to the tune of 114 million; its shares traded at Rs 13, Cargills Ceylon 110,000 shares crossed for Rs 86 million; its shares sold at Rs 786, CT Holdings 88000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 58 million; its shares sold at Rs 657, Royal Ceramics one million shares crossed for Rs 46.5 million; its shares sold at Rs 46.50, JKH 1.1 million shares crossed for Rs 46 million; its shares sold at Rs 21.60 and Haylays 150,000 shares crossed for Rs 28.50 million; its shares sold at Rs 190."
