    "chunk_size_bytes": 810,
    "chunk_text": "Under international human rights law, states are obligated to take steps to the \u201cmaximum of their available resources\u201d to progressively realize the rights to health, education, social security, and an adequate standard of living, among other economic, social, and cultural rights. States are obliged not only to act individually, but also through international assistance and cooperation. This necessarily implicates states\u2019 fiscal practices and tax policies domestically and in international fora.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka\u2019s economic quagmire makes clear that growth alone is not enough to fulfill human rights,\u201d Saadoun said. \u201cThe government should finally establish a progressive tax system and use its income so that it adequately funds education and other public services that benefit all Sri Lankans.\u201d"
