    "chunk_text": "More solutions \u2026\n\nMy Beauty Tips last week on \u2018Solutions for Fine Lines and Wrinkles,\u2019 did bring in a lot of comments, with some readers wanting me to highlight a few more solutions.\n\nMassage a small amount of extra virgin olive oil onto your clean face and leave it on overnight to allow deep absorption.\n\nFor an enhanced skin-soothing effect, mix olive oil with a few drops of essential oil (like lavender) before application.\n\nMash half an avocado to create a smooth paste and apply it as a mask on your face and leave it on for 15-20 minutes before rinsing.\n\nUse 02-03 times per week for a consistent boost of hydration and nourishment.\n\nFor added hydration, mix the avocado paste with a teaspoon of honey or yoghurt.\n\nMash a ripe banana into a smooth paste and apply it evenly on your face and leave on for 15-20 minutes before rinsing with lukewarm water.\n\nUse this treatment 02-03 times a week in order to reduce the appearance of fine lines and for soft and supple skin.\n\nYou can mix the banana paste with a small amount of yoghurt for an extra moisturising boost, along with probiotic benefits.\n\nWhisk one egg white, until it becomes frothy, and then apply it evenly to face and leave on for 15-20 minutes before rinsing with cool water.\n\nUse it 02-03 times per week to achieve a firmer skin texture.\n\nFor an extra tightening effect, combine the egg white with a few drops of lemon juice\u2014but always follow with sunscreen to protect your skin.\n\nBrew a cup of green tea and let it cool completely and then use it as a toner by applying it to your face with a cotton pad.\n\nIf possible, use daily for a refreshing boost that will keep your skin youthful and clear.\n\nFor added benefits, repurpose the used green tea bags as a cool compress for tired or puffy eyes.\n\nBlend 1/2 cucumber into a smooth paste and mix it with 01 tablespoon yoghurt and apply the mixture to your face and leave it on for 15-20 minutes before rinsing it off with lukewarm water."
